# It's Only Love, verse (figure 73.2)
# Twelve bars, AAB: the first four-bar phrase is played twice (his "2X"). The chromatic bassline
# C B B-flat F puts the e chord in 6/4 position over B; after the F Pollack types "...", and the
# bass G under the next two bars is added from the chord roots.
# Figures: the 4-3 suspension over G (resolving on beat 3), the augmented fifth on the second G,
# and the 6-5 appoggiatura over the C in the second phrase, each in a split bar.
#? Bass octave (C3 down to F2) is a choice; the G bass in bars 3-4 is added.
